From c4e116220aacea3bbffe50fa1a84ea4fec3a4d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iOS 10: rw-lock upgrade fix, getattrlistbulk, persona, kqueue
 wakeups, display probes

- lck_rw_lock_shared_to_exclusive: with other readers (or an upgrade or
  interlock pending) the assembly fast path jumped to
  lck_rw_lock_shared_gen, which took another read hold and returned
  "upgraded"; callers then modified vm_maps held only shared.  Go to the
  C upgrade path instead.  Only shows with real read contention, which
  iOS 10's many workqueue threads produce.
- getattrlistbulk (461): directory enumeration for launchd and others,
  built on getattrlist_internal and an extended readdir.
- persona (494): no process has a persona.  Other unimplemented
  iOS 10-numbered calls (445+) fail with ENOTSUP instead of SIGSYS.
- kevent: a Mach port knote added or re-enabled while a message is
  already queued wakes the kqueue (nothing else would).
- Framebuffer client: iOS 10's IOMobileFramebuffer opens the display
  with selectors iOS 7 never used; answer the plain scalar ones with
  success (iOS 10 only), and log calls and results on serial.
- Serial diagnostics: user data aborts, the crashing thread's backtrace
  on exit by signal, backboardd/SpringBoard thread states.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0123xbco8JF8tibbBMLmXceV
